  "description": "Aire starts with a Ventus Series hybrid frame that features Rider Optimized Geometry specifically designed to assure a proper and comfortable fit. Most importantly, Aire features a gender neutral step-thru designed frame that makes it easier to dismount when swinging a leg around the rear wheel is not desired or not possible. All Ventus Series models are ideally suited to a wide range of uses including commuting, fitness riding, recreational riding and good old fashioned errand running. Unlike its Solum Series counterparts, Aire uses a rigid steel fork with disc mounts to increase pedal efficiency by preventing energy loss associated with excess fork movement. Aire comes complete with a Shimano 21 speed drive train that includes EZ Fire shifters. Its wheelset is made from Pivit alloy 28h disc hubs laced to DC-27 700c alloy double wall rims and all weather stopping is made possible thanks to a pair of Tektro Aries mechanical disc brakes.\nHaro Ventus Hybrid Step-Thru frame, Rider Optimized Geometry, hydroformed alloy tubing, chainstay disc brake mount\nHaro Ventus steel fork with disc brake mount\nShimano TY-301 crankset, 48/38/28t, sealed cartridge BB\nShimano TY-510 Dual Pull front derailleur\nShimano Altus RD-M310-L rear derailleur\nShimano Tourney ST-EF-500 7-spd EZ Fire shifters\nPivit alloy disc 28h hubs w/ Alex DC-26 700c alloy DW rims\nPivit alloy 9 deg. sweep flat-bar & forged stem\nTektro Aries mechanical disc brakes\nPivit 2-Bolt seat post w/ zero offset",
